  "instance_name": "historical_event_american_reconstruction",
  "label": "American Reconstruction",
  "description": "The Reconstruction era (1865–1877) followed the American Civil War and involved efforts to reintegrate the Southern states into the Union and to address the status of formerly enslaved people. This period was marked by political turmoil, violence, and the rise of white supremacist groups. The top image, while not depicting Reconstruction, can be used symbolically to represent the suffering and sacrifice of African Americans during this time, which is a key part of American history. The meme's use of the image in this context is an implicit reference to this period.",
